>In several games I've given up looking.  But there must be some way
>to discover it's general locale, like (Quest level +/- 3) or something
>like that?  I saw a spoiler file that listed it as always at level 10,
>but I know this to be false.  Does it simply not exist in some games?

The Fort is located somewhere between level 10 and the Medusa Level
(both NOT included, so the spoiler you saw was definately incorrect).
There is no way to tell where it is more precisely. I THINK the way it
is determined is on-the-fly: it is the only level whose place is not
determined at game-start. Whenever you enter a new level between
mentioned levels, the game looks if there is a treasure vault on that
level. If so, there is a chance (2/3 or 1/3, I believe, but I'm not
sure), that the portal is created in THAT vault.

Thus, it is in theory possible that there will be NO portal, but the
chance is slim, since there must be on the average some 6 vaults or so
that are eligeble for a portal.

